    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The change adds Glm4ForCausalLM to architecture dispatch and supplies its configuration and model constructors. Config.from_directory can consequently select GLM4 instead of rejecting its architecture name.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5d16ebfbf5d34f418732e61c9bd7a7e0",
          "call_36bc6d919b494d448036a7c0f1ae34b6"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "GLM4 is expressed through existing modules: separate attention projections, fused-source gate/up projections, four norms per block and GPTJ-style rotary embeddings. Registration and construction are complementary edits; neither alone provides the complete factory path.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5d16ebfbf5d34f418732e61c9bd7a7e0",
          "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
          "call_c1fc037fc14747cbb5be8588aac77a69"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Reusing these primitives avoids a separate GLM execution implementation, but also exposes GLM checkpoints to the existing partial-RoPE frequency-read concern.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
          "call_79d0725509684d85b71542db1c12e009",
          "call_e3c7714d314549c5b78dd5afc0071cb0"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "All six inspected GLM4-family configurations select the new registration. Representative tensor headers agree with its projection dimensions and checkpoint names; this establishes structural correspondence, not successful loading, conversion or generation.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_c2ba4eaabacb4ad4b49642133f7ea581",
          "call_febf46aea77d47b396a184e14fa8fa79",
          "call_6f25a6e090e14bc5ba60fa6ee3232014",
          "call_24b483487e5f41d48f8d95269723b82c",
