    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "GLM4 construction, precision and checkpoint mapping",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Glm4Config requires hidden size, query-head count, intermediate size, RMS epsilon and layer count. Missing KV-head count defaults to query-head count; missing or zero head_dim falls back to hidden_size // num_attention_heads. Tied embeddings default to false, and a supplied hidden_act must be silu. The shared RoPE reader carries theta, scaling, partial rotary factor and context limits, now with GPTJ style.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_36bc6d919b494d448036a7c0f1ae34b6",
              "call_50e52904d1bb463f95ed5fffcee4e1e3",
              "call_2693942068a44bcb954b4132f9bdcc6c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The module sequence is embedding, indexed transformer blocks, final RMSNorm and lm_head. Within each block, input_layernorm precedes attention, post_self_attn_layernorm follows attention before residual addition, post_attention_layernorm precedes the MLP, and post_mlp_layernorm follows it before the second residual addition. Both branches receive input norms, so this construction does not enter TransformerBlock's uninitialized-y case for a branch without a norm.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_0ca37040fdf84b38a3260aef2d84691f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Embedding defaults to FP32 output, establishing the residual stream. TransformerBlock explicitly requests FP16 pre-normalized branch inputs. GLM4 requests FP32 post-norm outputs and FP32 MLP down-projection output, while keeping gate/up intermediates FP16. The final norm returns FP16 for the output projection. Thus it uses the parent's new linear-output precision facility without enabling the incompatible FP32 MLP-intermediate setting.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_a079c53d3c1049eca5b991d17c98d912",
              "call_0ca37040fdf84b38a3260aef2d84691f",
              "call_c175e70ee0d444efbe9e8d5a6d7e382c",
              "call_c1fc037fc14747cbb5be8588aac77a69",
              "call_3f6ce21b509b44e8a7c696390ac0b0cc"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Attention declares Q/K/V/O matrices with shapes [QD,H], [KD,H], [KD,H] and [H,QD]. GatedMLP first offers separate gate/up keys, then uses gate_up_proj as a fused source: rows [0,I) supply gate and [I,2I) supply up. Linear.load_fp16 slices that source along its first axis. Optional individual projection biases are loaded without an attention_bias constructor switch, covering the inspected 9B Q/K/V biases.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_3e334f7374e74b6a83e012515d868a1d",
              "call_c1fc037fc14747cbb5be8588aac77a69",
              "call_3f6ce21b509b44e8a7c696390ac0b0cc",
              "call_dd96e20bf0cf48ce8cc6c259ce7745b8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The fused gate/up mechanism retains its existing prohibition on MLP slicing when intermediate_size exceeds MAX_MLP_INTERMEDIATE=55296. This constant is documented as a practical single-GPU quantization limit. Both GLM widths, 23040 and 13696, remain below it; the new call does not bypass the guard.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c1fc037fc14747cbb5be8588aac77a69",
              "call_1c982ff3441741c89c0ee3bfc0692f5e",
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_c2ba4eaabacb4ad4b49642133f7ea581",
              "call_6f25a6e090e14bc5ba60fa6ee3232014"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "zai-org/GLM-4-32B-0414, zai-org/GLM-4-32B-Base-0414 and zai-org/GLM-Z1-32B-0414 each declare H=6144, I=23040, 61 layers, 48 query heads, two KV heads and D=128. Each agrees with the constructor's dimensions and SiLU requirement, explicitly disables tied embeddings and attention biases, and supplies a 32768-position limit. The GLM-4-32B first-shard header matches embedding [151552,6144], Q/O [6144,6144], K/V [256,6144], fused gate/up [46080,6144], down [6144,23040] and four norm vectors of length 6144.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c2ba4eaabacb4ad4b49642133f7ea581",
              "call_febf46aea77d47b396a184e14fa8fa79",
              "call_24b483487e5f41d48f8d95269723b82c",
              "call_f2c8a61e42a74e12b9946b24a839c9d1",
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "zai-org/GLM-4-9B-0414 and zai-org/GLM-Z1-9B-0414 each declare H=4096, I=13696, 40 layers, 32 query heads, two KV heads and D=128. Both fit the constructor's dimensions and defaults, with explicit SiLU, untied embeddings, attention_bias=true and a 32768-position limit. The inspected GLM-4-9B header matches Q/O [4096,4096], K/V [256,4096], fused gate/up [27392,4096], down [4096,13696], four 4096-element norms, and Q/K/V biases of lengths 4096/256/256.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6f25a6e090e14bc5ba60fa6ee3232014",
              "call_ed3433c433654ce4a0a6ce662f7383be",
              "call_dd96e20bf0cf48ce8cc6c259ce7745b8",
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "zai-org/GLM-Z1-Rumination-32B-0414 retains the 6144/23040 widths, 61 layers and 48 query heads, but supplies eight KV heads and a 131072-position limit. These values are read rather than replaced by the other 32B models' defaults. Its inspected first-layer header matches K/V [1024,6144], with the same Q/O, fused MLP and norm shapes as the other 32B layout. No inspected tensor name in these representative header portions lacks a corresponding loading path.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_798c76bbcc0345f1b6297762b432a0cd",
              "call_6ba0116097b4485b8ee9ff926b59e994",
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_3f6ce21b509b44e8a7c696390ac0b0cc",
              "call_c175e70ee0d444efbe9e8d5a6d7e382c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All six configurations explicitly use head_dim=128, partial_rotary_factor=0.5, rope_theta=10000 and rms_norm_eps=1e-5. RoPE therefore builds 32 inverse frequencies for 64 rotated channels. GPTJ pairs adjacent channels rather than split halves, rotating the first 64 channels and copying the remaining 64. The native source still reads inv_freq[t] before deciding whether a thread only copies an unrotated pair.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c2ba4eaabacb4ad4b49642133f7ea581",
              "call_febf46aea77d47b396a184e14fa8fa79",
              "call_6f25a6e090e14bc5ba60fa6ee3232014",
              "call_24b483487e5f41d48f8d95269723b82c",
              "call_ed3433c433654ce4a0a6ce662f7383be",
              "call_798c76bbcc0345f1b6297762b432a0cd",
              "call_79d0725509684d85b71542db1c12e009",
              "call_e3c7714d314549c5b78dd5afc0071cb0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library scalar transcription reproduced the three projection layouts and query-heads-per-KV-head ratios 24, 16 and 6. It also counted 64 launched x indices versus 32 frequencies, leaving source-level indices 32\u201363 outside the frequency array for every inspected configuration. This was arithmetic validation, not execution of RoPE or a GPU memory test.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_74d5348874e64bab91acb51928ab3e62"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "prepare_inputs retains input_ids in params and delegates to prepare_for_attn, exactly as the inspected Llama, Phi3, Gemma and DeciLM callers do. It omits no additional caller-side guard present in those implementations. The shared helper defaults to cache-free FlashAttention, rejects caches in cache-free modes, validates the batch-shaped cached mode and rejects unknown modes.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1ad9eb442d4d443abcd80afa1e7df56d",
              "call_1173ce2a8bfe4f7c9723db310da5fa32",
              "call_91480880654f4117a689d55850f84529",
              "call_8fb3571bde9b42c9b48de17792617afb",
              "call_624878fab22f4aeca1bd9dc3667d9d6f",
              "call_72abdc16006f4b1badefa6c6ee5810cb",
              "call_3e334f7374e74b6a83e012515d868a1d"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
