        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "GLM4's partial rotary configuration reaches the inherited unconditional frequency read outside the rotated-channel guard. The task leaves this native code unchanged.",
        "trigger": "Attention executes native RoPE for any inspected GLM4-family configuration: head_dim=128 and partial_rotary_factor=0.5.",
        "expected_behavior": "Threads copying the unrotated channels should not index beyond the 32-element inverse-frequency array.",
        "actual_behavior": "rope launches 64 x threads and rope_kernel evaluates inv_freq[t] before its rotation/copy branch. Source-level indices 32\u201363 exceed the array. The inspected SDPA, cache-free FlashAttention and cached FlashAttention methods all call RoPE.apply, which calls ext.rope; actual compiled GPU consequences remain untested.",
